        {
          "key": "audit_criteria",
          "type": "checklist",
          "label": "Temperature audit criteria",
          "items": [
            "Food, batch, case, equipment, and sample point are clear",
            "Instrument identity and readiness record are present",
            "Target comes from a current policy reference",
            "Reading includes time, value, and unit",
            "Repeat-reading requirement was addressed",
            "Product quantity and exposure facts are recorded",
            "Disposition is within documented authority",
            "Equipment issue has a linked response ticket",
            "Follow-up reading has owner and due time",
            "Qualified review closes unresolved disposition"
          ]
        },
        {
          "key": "audit_boundary",
          "type": "notice",
          "label": "Audit conclusion boundary",
          "guidance": "This form records measurements and decisions under the current procedure; it does not set temperature limits or certify food safety or regulatory compliance. Do not guess a target, exposure duration, or disposition. Stop affected activity when policy requires and route illness, safety, and final product decisions to the qualified food-safety reviewer under applicable requirements."
        }
